        "People often confuse plantar fasciitis with a heel spur, but they aren't quite the same thing. A heel spur is a small bony growth that can form on the heel bone over time, often as a result of long-standing plantar fasciitis, but many people with heel spurs have no pain at all, and many people with significant heel pain have no spur visible on imaging. This is why Heel Spur Treatment Dubai searches often lead people to the same underlying issue: the plantar fascia itself, not the bone."
