      anatomyTitle: "Understanding Cervical Spine Anatomy",
      anatomyParagraph: "The cervical spine is made up of seven small bones, called cervical vertebrae, stacked on top of one another. Between each vertebra sits a disc that acts as a cushion, and small joints on either side allow the neck to bend, rotate, and tilt. Nerves branch out from the spinal cord through narrow openings between these vertebrae, carrying signals to the shoulders, arms, and hands.",
      degenerationTitle: "How Degeneration Develops",
      degenerationParagraph: "Over time, the discs in the neck can lose height and hydration, a process known as disc degeneration. Patients researching cervical disc degeneration Dubai or cervical degenerative disc disease Dubai are typically describing this exact stage of the condition. The joints may also develop small bony growths called bone spurs, as the body tries to stabilize areas of extra movement. According to the Mayo Clinic, these changes are a normal part of aging and are present to some degree in most people over 60, though not everyone develops symptoms.",
      slippedDiscTitle: "Cervical Spondylosis vs. a Slipped Disc",
      slippedDiscParagraph: "People often confuse cervical spondylosis with a slipped or herniated disc. Spondylosis refers to the broader degenerative process affecting bones, joints, and discs over years. A herniated disc, on the other hand, is a specific event where the inner material of a disc pushes outward, which can sometimes happen on top of existing spondylosis and press on a nearby nerve.",
      earlyTreatmentTitle: "Why Early Cervical Spondylosis Treatment Dubai Matters",
      earlyTreatmentParagraph: "Many people ignore mild neck stiffness, assuming it will pass on its own. While mild cases often do settle with simple care, catching the condition early allows for better management of posture, movement habits, and muscle strength — reducing the chance of the problem progressing to nerve compression or spinal cord compression in more advanced stages."
